{
  "#": "Defaults shipped with dic.  Do not edit: this file is replaced on upgrade.  Write ~/.config/fac/providers.json and ~/.config/fac/models.json (or point $DIC_MODELS at a file) instead; their entries are merged over these, key by key, so an id may be reused to change one setting.  Keys beginning with '#' are comments.",

  "#ids": "An id is a '+'-separated chain, weakest first: 'groq+qwen' is the entry 'qwen' layered on the entry 'groq'.  Entries with \"abstract\": true are providers or mixins; they cannot be used with -m, only inherited from.  Chains nobody wrote down work too: 'thinking-high+anthropic+sonnet'.",

  "#cache": "A cache is a purchase, so it is off unless a model prices it: dic sends a cache_control block only when --cache names a TTL that the model's own price table rates.  Every anthropic+* entry therefore states in.cache_read, in.cache_write.5m and in.cache_write.1h at the published multipliers -- 0.1x the input rate to read, 1.25x for a five minute write and 2x for an hour -- and every other provider states none, so openrouter+* can never be billed for a cache dic cannot rate.",

  "groq": {
    "abstract": true,
    "api_base": "https://api.groq.com/openai/v1",
    "api_key_name": "GROQ_API_KEY",
    "pricing_url": {"url": "https://groq.com/pricing/"},
    "sync": {"fetcher": "openai"}
  },

