  "#tiers": "OpenAI prices a call by service tier and by context length, and the two are independent axes: the most specific rule wins and neither implies the other, so every combination is a rule of its own.  flex is half the standard rate, fast (formerly priority) is double, ultrafast is six times.  Over 272k input tokens the input rate doubles, cached input included, and the output rate is multiplied by 1.5.  fast and priority are both written at the same rate because the response is what is billed and either spelling may come back.  Cached input is priced here so that a cache hit is not billed at the plain input rate; a cache write is not, because no OpenAI adaptor reports one.  batch is not: dic has no batch transport yet.",

